# Cloudflare Pages: exclude the graph database from the asset upload.
#
# Cloudflare Pages/Workers caps a single static asset at 25 MiB; graph.db.gz is
# larger, which fails the deploy. On Cloudflare the app loads the graph from the
# CDN instead (VITE_GRAPH_DB_URL -> Cloudflare R2), so the file isn't needed in
# the uploaded output. See docs/CDN_HOSTING.md.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ to the root of dist/, so this file lands at
# dist/.assetsignore automatically. It is Cloudflare-specific; GitHub Pages and
# local dev ignore it and keep serving public/graph.db.gz same-origin.
#
# Patterns are gitignore-style, relative to the output root.
graph.db*
